- [ ] Phase start time and duration tracked
- [ ] Phase transitions logged for debugging

## Problem
Pods show 0/1 Ready for extended periods (10+ minutes for TensorRT-LLM) even when the model is actually loaded and serving. This is due to initialDelaySeconds on readiness probes, but this isn't communicated to operators.

## Implementation Details

### File: operators/ai-model-operator/internal/controller/aimodel_controller.go

1. Extract readiness probe config and calculate expected ready time:
```go
func (r *AIModelReconciler) getReadinessInfo(pod *corev1.Pod) *ReadinessInfo {
    if pod == nil || pod.Spec.NodeName == "" {
        return nil
    }

    for _, container := range pod.Spec.Containers {
        if container.Name == "kserve-container" && container.ReadinessProbe != nil {
            probe := container.ReadinessProbe

            // Find container start time
            var startTime *time.Time
            for _, cs := range pod.Status.ContainerStatuses {
                if cs.Name == "kserve-container" && cs.State.Running != nil {
                    startTime = &cs.State.Running.StartedAt.Time
                    break
                }
            }

            if startTime == nil {
                return nil
            }

            readyTime := startTime.Add(time.Duration(probe.InitialDelaySeconds) * time.Second)
            remaining := time.Until(readyTime)

            return &ReadinessInfo{
                InitialDelay:     probe.InitialDelaySeconds,
                ExpectedReadyAt:  readyTime,
                TimeRemaining:    remaining,
                ProbeStarted:     remaining <= 0,
            }
        }
    }
    return nil
}
```

2. Add to status message during Initializing phase:
```go
if phase == PhaseInitializing {
    readiness := r.getReadinessInfo(pod)
    if readiness != nil && !readiness.ProbeStarted {
        aimodel.Status.Message = fmt.Sprintf(
            "Model loaded, waiting for readiness probe (starts in %s)",
            readiness.TimeRemaining.Round(time.Second))
    } else if readiness != nil && readiness.ProbeStarted {
        aimodel.Status.Message = "Readiness probe running, waiting for healthy response"
    }
}
```

3. Add to AIModel status struct:
```go
type AIModelStatus struct {
    // ... existing fields
    ReadinessInfo *ReadinessInfo `json:"readinessInfo,omitempty"`
}

type ReadinessInfo struct {
    InitialDelay    int32     `json:"initialDelay"`
    ExpectedReadyAt time.Time `json:"expectedReadyAt,omitempty"`
    TimeRemaining   string    `json:"timeRemaining,omitempty"`
}
```

### Testing
- Unit test: Readiness time calculation
- Integration test: Deploy model with long probe delay, verify status shows countdown

### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Status shows time remaining until readiness probe starts
- [ ] Status indicates when probe is actively checking
- [ ] Operators understand why pod shows 0/1 during initialization

