## Problem
When a model pod can't schedule, the AIModel status just shows 'Deploying' with no indication of why. Operators must dig through pod events to find scheduling errors.

## Implementation Details

### File: operators/ai-model-operator/internal/controller/aimodel_controller.go

1. Add scheduling status to AIModel status:
```go
// In api/v1alpha1/aimodel_types.go
type AIModelStatus struct {
    Phase            string             `json:"phase"`
    Message          string             `json:"message,omitempty"`
    SchedulingStatus *SchedulingStatus  `json:"schedulingStatus,omitempty"`
    // ... existing fields
}

type SchedulingStatus struct {
    Scheduled      bool   `json:"scheduled"`
    BlockedReason  string `json:"blockedReason,omitempty"`
    BlockedMessage string `json:"blockedMessage,omitempty"`
    NodeName       string `json:"nodeName,omitempty"`
}
```

2. In reconciler, check pod scheduling status:
```go
func (r *AIModelReconciler) getSchedulingStatus(ctx context.Context, pod *corev1.Pod) *SchedulingStatus {
    status := &SchedulingStatus{}

    if pod.Spec.NodeName != "" {
        status.Scheduled = true
        status.NodeName = pod.Spec.NodeName
        return status
    }

    // Check pod conditions for scheduling failure
    for _, cond := range pod.Status.Conditions {
        if cond.Type == corev1.PodScheduled && cond.Status == corev1.ConditionFalse {
            status.Scheduled = false
            status.BlockedReason = cond.Reason
            status.BlockedMessage = r.parseSchedulingMessage(cond.Message)
            return status
        }
    }

    return status
}

func (r *AIModelReconciler) parseSchedulingMessage(msg string) string {
    // Parse K8s scheduling message into human-readable form
    // "0/6 nodes are available: 2 Insufficient cpu..." ->
    // "Insufficient CPU: need 8 cores, largest available node has 7.3 cores"
    // This requires querying node resources
}
```

3. Update status message to include scheduling info:
```go
if !schedulingStatus.Scheduled {
    aimodel.Status.Message = fmt.Sprintf("Waiting for scheduling: %s", schedulingStatus.BlockedMessage)
}
```

### Testing
